1
00:06:47,142 --> 00:06:53,142
Kurt & Courtney is a documentary, music film directed by Nick Broomfield.

2
00:13:34,285 --> 00:13:40,285
After rocker Kurt Cobain's death, ruled a suicide, a film
crew arrives in Seattle to make a documentary.

3
00:20:21,428 --> 00:20:27,428
Director Nick Broomfield talks to lots of people.

4
00:27:08,571 --> 00:27:14,571
Portraits emerge: a shy, slight Kurt, weary of touring, embarrassed by fame, hooked on
heroin; an out-going Courtney, dramatic, controlling, moving from groupie to star.

5
00:33:55,714 --> 00:34:01,714
Self - Interviewer, played by Nick Broomfield.

6
00:40:42,857 --> 00:40:48,857
Self, played by Dylan Carlson.

7
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
Self (archive footage), played by Kurt Cobain.

8
00:54:17,142 --> 00:54:23,142
Self, played by El Duce.

9
01:01:04,285 --> 01:01:10,285
Self, played by Larry Flynt.

10
01:07:51,428 --> 01:07:57,428
Self, played by Tom Grant.

11
01:14:38,571 --> 01:14:44,571
Kurt & Courtney is a 1998 British documentary film by Nick Broomfield investigating the circumstances
surrounding the death of Kurt Cobain, and allegations of Courtney Love's involvement in it.

12
01:21:25,714 --> 01:21:31,714
The film explores themes of singing, embryo,
living under the bridge, music rights.

13
01:28:12,857 --> 01:28:18,857
The tone is emotional.
